ubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"a2741399fe5057df4df1170b66cb0593fad4c9f762dd107526fbd2165feac7c5","event_uuid":"8dd7ae9a-bcd6-49c9-bb3f-2cb827ff1043","position":{"commit_sha":"aa886417a59c1a2d7687a1ca5b419d60a2977ef7","position":"1794567689371772001-8dd7ae9a-bcd6-49c9-bb3f-2cb827ff1043"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"3d705fec-b472-45ca-b9ca-e9472648a082","comments":[],"created_at":1794547697775543001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2603c90a-ba15-43e2-838d-86e22d647e3e","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561"}],"description":"## Problem\n`_run_plan_review` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py`, about line 625) runs `_apply_review_floors` only when `engine == \"pipeline\"`. Under the agentic engine, these steps are skipped:\n- the Pass-3 rising floor;\n- the completion floor;\n- the drift floor (`drift_floor.maybe_apply`, which can downgrade BLOCK to PASS through `_recompute_verdict_after_drop`);\n- the consistency cross-checks (`xcheck.maybe_apply_contradiction` and `maybe_apply_comment_trail`, which rewrite `verdict[\"blocking\"]`);\n- fix-unit grouping.\n\nSo for the same plan material and findings, the two engines can sign different verdict strings and blocking lists.\n\nThe code comment cites ADR 0123, but `docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md` documents only the Layer-1 floor and claimability running first under both engines. It does not say that the post-dispatch tail is pipeline-only, or that the drift floor's convergence (a code-drift re-review of an unchanged plan converging back to PASS) does not apply to agentic reviews.\n\n## Decision\nThe steps stay pipeline-only, and ADR 0123 is amended to say so and why (operator direction, 2026-11-13). No behavior change.\n\nWhat `_run_plan_review` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py`) runs only when `engine == \"pipeline\"`, checked at ca3768c970d:\n\nPost-dispatch tail (`_apply_review_floors`):\n- Rising floor and completion floor: drop surfaced **advisory** findings only; the completion floor is inert unless `verify.completion_floor_active`.\n- Drift floor (`drift_floor.maybe_apply`): on a plan-unchanged, code-drifted re-review, drops a **novel** finding from the blocking or advisory list when its citations miss the drifted files, then re-derives the verdict string, so it can turn BLOCK into PASS.\n- Cross-checks (`xcheck.maybe_apply_contradiction`, `maybe_apply_comment_trail`): drop contradicted or already-resolved findings from **both** lists and re-derive the verdict string; inert unless their `verify.*_xcheck_active` flags are on.\n- Fix-unit grouping: one LLM sub-call that stamps co-cited blocking findings for the CLI; changes no bucket, count or verdict.\n\nPre-dispatch shortcuts (already commented in code as pipeline-only, but not in the ADR):\n- Idempotent attestation reuse (`reuse.idempotent_reuse`), BLOCK verdict reuse (`reuse.verdict_reuse`) and progressive drift refresh (`orchestrator.drift_refresh`). Each reuses or re-signs a **pipeline** attestation or verdict, so under agentic each review runs the agent afresh.\n\nEvery tail step only removes or stamps findings; none adds a finding or turns PASS into BLOCK.\n\n## Plan\n1. Amend `docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md` §6 (\"Invariants both engines keep\") with a bullet stating that the post-dispatch tail (5 steps) and the 3 pre-dispatch shortcuts run only under the pipeline engine, and why:\n   - the operator decided on 2026-11-09 (§3) that an agentic verdict blocks only on `blocker` findings, with `major`, `minor` and `trivial` advisory. The drift floor and cross-checks remove findings from the blocking list, so running them on agentic verdicts would override that decision;\n   - the rising and completion floors only thin advisory findings, and fix-unit grouping only stamps blocking findings for display; none changes an agentic verdict, and each is tuned to pipeline findings;\n   - the 3 shortcuts reuse or re-sign a pipeline attestation or verdict, which an agentic review must not inherit;\n   - each tail step only removes or stamps findings, so skipping them can keep a BLOCK the tail would have dropped from the same agentic findings, but cannot turn a BLOCK into a PASS. This is relative to running the tail on the same agentic findings, not to the pipeline's verdict; the engines produce different finding sets. It is consistent with the epic's no-bypass invariant, which the attestation binding (§5) enforces.\n2. In the same bullet, state the consequence: ADR 0052 §2's re-review-stability contract (an unchanged, signed plan re-reviewed at a drifted HEAD yields no new blocking findings) is upheld by the drift floor, cross-checks and drift refresh, so it holds for the pipeline engine only. An agentic re-review after code drift runs the agent afresh and can surface new blocking findings.\n3. Add a 2026-11-13 dated line to ADR 0123's amendment section recording this.\n4. Add a dated 2026-11-13 note under `docs/adr/0052-plan-review-validation-consistency-and-re-review-stability.md` §2 saying the contract applies to the pipeline engine and pointing to ADR 0123 §6, so the contract's own home carries the scope.\n5. `docs/plan-review-gate.md` §\"Choosing an engine\": add 1 sentence saying the pipeline's reuse, drift refresh, post-review floors and cross-checks, and so ADR 0052's re-review stability, apply to the pipeline engine only.\n6. The ADR names the pinning test: `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic.py::test_post_dispatch_tail_runs_only_under_pipeline` asserts that `_apply_review_floors`, the single entry point for every tail step, runs for pipeline and never for an agentic review (floor-blocked, DET-passing and degraded). It pins the entry point, not each step; the ADR says so. Run that test.\n\nNo code, config key, env var or flag changes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] ADR 0123 §6 states that the post-dispatch tail (5 steps) and the 3 pre-dispatch shortcuts are pipeline-only, gives the reasons above, and states that ADR 0052 §2's re-review stability holds for the pipeline engine only; the amendment section carries a 2026-11-13 line.\n- [ ] ADR 0052 §2 carries a dated 2026-11-13 note scoping the contract to the pipeline engine.\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` §\"Choosing an engine\" says the reuse, drift refresh, floors, cross-checks and ADR 0052 re-review stability are pipeline-only.\n- [ ] The ADR names `test_post_dispatch_tail_runs_only_under_pipeline` as the test pinning the entry point, and that test passes.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md","reason":"pipeline-only tail and shortcuts, section 6 and amendment"},{"path":"docs/adr/0052-plan-review-validation-consistency-and-re-review-stability.md","reason":"scope note on section 2"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"Choosing an engine: pipeline-only steps"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a627b366-56a9-4169-b4cc-2517ebc9e1d6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5bd7-33ec-8630-440e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Agentic verdicts skip drift floor and cross-checks","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8c053e4c-175d-4d43-9810-3fa6c18a669f","8b52d3b9-e842-474b-a77b-85b225aa152b","3a18c415-d261-4b2c-a7e3-e774dd0ca36c","2c9632f3-9a43-4782-865e-e4e0617c86a0","654a53d6-1fa9-4dad-a2d5-76a4abeae314","c7a26307-ecbc-4d2c-a3af-35c842bf7536","89a7f078-4abb-4582-9d7f-e0e0bfcea9ee","968ff08c-e8fb-421b-8c87-45086d06e559","c34952b0-1d6b-409c-b285-9cb4cbb442ac","a627b366-56a9-4169-b4cc-2517ebc9e1d6","8dd7ae9a-bcd6-49c9-bb3f-2cb827ff1043"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794567689371772002,"uuid":"83b02198-f4c4-4b33-baf4-baeb79600894"}